  "worked_solution": "In this context, the area $A$ under the curve $y=p(t)$ over the interval $[0,9]$ represents the total number of kilowatt-hours of energy produced in the first nine hours.\n\nThe general formula for the trapezoidal rule states that\n\n$$\nA\u2248\\frac{1}{2}[p(a)+2(p({t}_{1})+p({t}_{2})+\u2026+p({t}_{n-1}))+p(b)]\u0394t,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is the number of trapezoids and $\u0394t=\\frac{b-a}{n}$ is the step size.\n\nHere, we have the following values:\n\n- The number of trapezoids is $n=3.$\n\n- The corresponding interval is $[0,9],$ so we have $a=0$ and $b=9.$\n\n- The step size is given by\n\n$$\n\u0394t=\\frac{b-a}{n}=\\frac{9-0}{3}=3.\n$$\n\nUsing the above values, the general formula becomes\n\n$$\nA\u2248\\frac{1}{2}[p(0)+2(p(3)+p(6))+p(9)]\\cdot 3.\n$$\n\nTo identify the function values, we now set up a table with the values of $t$ and $p(t):$\n\n| $t$ | $0$ | $3$ | $6$ | $9$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $p(t)$ | $0$ | $42$ | $48$ | $18$ |\n\nSubstituting the appropriate numbers into the above expression gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & \u2248\\frac{1}{2}[0+2(42+48)+18]\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[198]\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =297.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solar array produced $297$ kilowatt-hours of energy in the first nine hours.",
